;; A sheltered hollow under a stepped roof; a steady lift (columns 4-6)
;; rises from its floor to Q. West of it the homeward shaft (columns 1-3,
;; D50) falls from Q to a rose stone just above K's floor (1,9), and on
;; through a one-tile hole to E: the way home, readable before H5 and open
;; with it. Shut, the stone seals the shaft, so it cannot be climbed from E
;; (the reverse route SYSTEMS' replay found: wall kicks up E's west wall
;; into the shaft, then the lift).
(room
  region: cloudstair
  at: (7 -1)
  title: "Sheltered Seeds"
  intent: "seed creatures rest in a sheltered hollow below the last grass: a breath"
  bed: (wind 0.3 water 0 air 0.5 drone 0.3)
  light: 1
  sun: 1
  grid:
  ("#   ^^^##################"
   "#   ^^^   ###############"
   "#   ^^^     #############"
   "#   ^^^       ###########"
   "#   ^^^         #########"
   "#   ^^^           #######"
   "#   ^^^             #####"
   "#   ^^^                  "
   "#   ^^^                  "
   "#o  ^^^ |  ||  |  | |    "
   "# #######################")
  things: ((seed at: (12 9) count: 3)
           ;; the shaft's rose stone (D50): shut, the way home is sealed and
           ;; nothing climbs up the shaft from E; with H5 it opens as you come
           ;; down onto it, and the shaft falls on through to E
           (ring-stone at: (1 9) overtone: 5)
           (seed at: (5 5) count: 2))
  decor: auto)
